# A live folder's plug-in gets the HTTP status of every answer, not only 2xx: GitHub's 401 (signed out),
# 403 (rate limit, SSO) and 429 are how it knows to ask for a sign-in or to wait. On the engine the session
# fetch dropped every non-2xx answer as a failed request (status 0), so a signed-out enterprise folder said
# "GitHub can’t be reached" (16 Nov 2026). Status 0 stays for a request that got no answer.
budget rss=600
cra://debug?pluginFetch=${ORIGIN}/no-such-page
expect-log plugin fetch status=404 body=[0-9]+ chars
cra://debug?pluginFetch=${ORIGIN}/page.html
expect-log plugin fetch status=200 body=[0-9]+ chars
cra://debug?pluginFetch=http://127.0.0.1:9/
expect-log plugin fetch status=0 body=empty
